{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"I now have strong evidence. Let me verify the key facts:\n\nFrom e1 (Murakami Wikipedia):\n- Murakami born in **Fushimi-ku, Kyoto, Japan**\n- \"Growing up in Ashiya, near Kobe\"\n- Work translated into 50 languages (\u003e25 ✓)\n- 1Q84 published in Japan May 29, 2009; \"longlisted for the Man Asian Literary Prize in 2011\"\n\nThe Man Asian Literary Prize was established in 2007 (created in the 2000s ✓). 1Q84 was a contender (longlisted) for this prize. The English translation of 1Q84 was published in 2011 (in the 2010s ✓).\n\nNow I need to verify the second book: a book released the preceding year (2010) that won the Man Asian Literary Prize, whose author was born in Ashiya (where Murakami grew up). Let me confirm the 2011 Man Asian Literary Prize winner.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Man Asian Literary Prize 2011 winner\", \"Man Asian Literary Prize 2011 shortlist winner novel\", \"Man Asian Literary Prize 2011 awarded\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_4653cf0c9054499ea60d1f73","index":0,"type":"function"}]}}],"created":1789466378,"id":"chatcmpl-d24db651-5d8c-95fb-abf6-acff631dd06a","model":"glm-5.2","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":20408,"completion_tokens":253,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":20661,"cached_tokens":3712,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":3712},"prompt_cost":0.000000,"completion_cost":0.000000,"cache_cost":0.000000}}